  "method": "Two players on each isolated loopback Minecraft server issued native commands, clicked two overview and three item pages, inspected recipes and submitted a real four-line sign edit. A server-side probe checked the frozen fixture's expected keys, materials, metadata, menu state, native clicks, cursor and inventory. The independent protocol clients decoded every displayed slot and item caption on sampled views. Exact inputs were hashed again after clean shutdown.",
  "coverage": [
    "Ranked and tied authored groups; distinct labels and window headings; implicit, disabled, missing, denied, cross-bundle and empty groups. Missing or repaired icon, live member counts, canonical damaged item versus pristine display, native tooltip metadata.",
    "Ordered and deduplicated mixed exact/glob contributions, final exclusions, item primary groups and all-items. Forty-six implicit group keys, forty-seven stock items, multiple overview and item pages, hidden content, per-viewer item and group permissions.",
    "Direct and targeted opens, sender and recipient access, distinct missing/denied chat, preserved unrelated windows. Nested recipe navigation restores exact item and overview pages. The real private sign and typed global search return to the correct overview origin.",
    "Denied and authorized grants, upstream event cancellation, a changed tile, replaced view, permission revocation, invalid transactional content reload, valid reload invalidation and clean player stock.",
    "A blank original primary group resolves to default in browsing and actual command-completion responses, including independently denied and permitted players. Layout front pins real keys, ignores missing entries and rejects duplicate normalized keys. Declared and alphabetic remainders are paged under live config reload. Conditional contributions do not edit an existing group when configured to skip, and the first explicitly authored contribution can decorate an implicit or reserved group."
  ],
  "limits": "Native packet and server-state verification covers menu contents and interactions. Rendered appearance is reserved for the user.",
